            <ArticleTitle>Progressive bradycardia with increasing doses of dobutamine leading to stress echo interruption.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dobutamine stress testing is an important non-invasive method for evaluating patients with known or suspected coronary artery disease who are unable to adequately exercise. We present a case of a paradoxical, progressive bradycardia occurring with increasing doses of dobutamine that resulted in stress test interruption.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
